WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.213 --> 00:00:02.059
- I guess what I think veganism is...

00:00:02.059 --> 00:00:03.777
- I went to vegans for Dummies.

00:00:03.777 --> 00:00:05.193
- I don't know much about veganism,

00:00:05.193 --> 00:00:06.378
but what I do know...

00:00:06.378 --> 00:00:08.212
- (laughs) It sucks!

00:00:08.212 --> 00:00:10.551
(intense music)

00:00:15.875 --> 00:00:18.301
- Starting tomorrow, the
four of us will be vegans

00:00:18.301 --> 00:00:19.636
for the next thirty days.

00:00:19.636 --> 00:00:21.481
- I don't feel good about
being on a vegan diet.

00:00:21.481 --> 00:00:22.655
- Hell no. (laughs)

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.535
- What am I going to do with tofu?

00:00:24.535 --> 00:00:26.798
- I would probably suckle
directly from a cow's teat.

00:00:29.688 --> 00:00:31.119
- My diet now

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:33.408
is like whatever.

00:00:33.762 --> 00:00:36.002
- I don't know what I'm
going to do without cheese.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.304
- Yeah, I have some concerns.

00:00:37.304 --> 00:00:38.927
One, my sanity.

00:00:38.927 --> 00:00:39.984
- I just hate the thought of like

00:00:39.984 --> 00:00:41.525
restricting what I eat.

00:00:41.525 --> 00:00:42.577
- We're doing this for a month

00:00:42.577 --> 00:00:44.017
because we actually do want to really

00:00:44.017 --> 00:00:46.420
have the time to take this seriously

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.860
and learn about what
it means to be a vegan.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.602
- I wanna try a vegan diet maybe because

00:00:49.602 --> 00:00:51.493
that's the way of the future.

00:00:51.493 --> 00:00:53.479
- I feel like this'll be a good cleanse

00:00:53.479 --> 00:00:54.802
for my body.

00:00:54.802 --> 00:00:55.917
- To say, at the end of this,

00:00:55.917 --> 00:00:58.993
that I will go vegan, very slim chances.

00:00:58.993 --> 00:01:00.537
However, maybe I come out of this

00:01:00.537 --> 00:01:02.499
and get in the habit of cooking more

00:01:02.499 --> 00:01:05.524
and just doing better things
to my body in general.

00:01:05.703 --> 00:01:07.481
- It's day one, and Ryan already cheated.

00:01:07.481 --> 00:01:09.767
- [Ryan] Alright, so she just recorded me

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.090
saying I'm eating this...

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:12.610
- I'm eating salad all day.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:14.028
We are going to meet with the nutritionist

00:01:14.028 --> 00:01:15.780
and get some advice because

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.661
none of us know how to be good vegans.

00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:20.807
- I work out a lot, and I'm
really concerned about protein.

00:01:20.807 --> 00:01:22.642
- You actually don't have
to worry too much about it

00:01:22.642 --> 00:01:24.649
because a lot of the grains
in the plant-based foods

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:26.809
that you're eating, that
replace the protein,

00:01:26.809 --> 00:01:28.842
so the grains, the legumes, the beans...

00:01:28.842 --> 00:01:31.429
Those foods have a lot of protein in them.

00:01:31.429 --> 00:01:33.392
- [Jared] Is there anything
vegan that's delicious?

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:34.495
- Yeah, there's tons of stuff that's vegan

00:01:34.495 --> 00:01:35.364
that's delicious.
- [Jared] Like what?

00:01:35.364 --> 00:01:36.966
- Like avocados are delicious,

00:01:36.966 --> 00:01:38.766
I like most fruits and vegetables, so...

00:01:38.766 --> 00:01:40.786
- Great. Thank you so much!

00:01:40.786 --> 00:01:41.507
- You're welcome!

00:01:41.507 --> 00:01:42.923
- This has been very, very illuminating.

00:01:42.923 --> 00:01:45.047
- I am no longer happy when I'm hungry.

00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:46.336
And that's kind of sad.

00:01:46.336 --> 00:01:48.731
- It's really sad.

00:01:48.731 --> 00:01:49.881
- [Jared] Yeah, it's a little sad.

00:01:49.881 --> 00:01:51.971
- [Jen] Three hot dogs at work,

00:01:51.971 --> 00:01:53.991
- [Jared] Three hot
dogs, but we're getting

00:01:53.991 --> 00:01:55.347
vegan hot dogs...

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:56.009
- Vegan hot dogs.

00:01:56.009 --> 00:01:57.913
- Getting a chili dog, must be nice.

00:01:59.663 --> 00:02:00.493
But I'm not afforded that luxury

00:02:00.493 --> 00:02:02.676
because BuzzFeed is
hell-bent on punishing me

00:02:02.676 --> 00:02:04.056
for no reason.

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:05.311
- We're about two weeks into being vegan

00:02:05.311 --> 00:02:08.213
and I feel pretty much the same.

00:02:08.213 --> 00:02:10.314
I think I'm just a tired
person to begin with,

00:02:10.314 --> 00:02:13.750
so any other additional tiredness

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.038
just kinds of blends in.

00:02:15.038 --> 00:02:17.210
- It's definitely been
like a roller coaster,

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.417
both mentally and physically.

00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:20.588
Over the past couple of days,

00:02:20.588 --> 00:02:22.933
I've been like pushing
myself to go out to different

00:02:22.933 --> 00:02:24.408
vegan restaurants and try

00:02:24.408 --> 00:02:28.186
a bunch of awesome vegan cuisine.

00:02:28.378 --> 00:02:29.817
- I've actually started
paying a lot more attention

00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:30.793
to what I eat,

00:02:30.793 --> 00:02:32.337
and I've been eating a
lot more fresh veggies,

00:02:32.337 --> 00:02:34.868
and I've been eating a
lot more varied foods.

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:36.436
- I feel really tired all the time.

00:02:36.436 --> 00:02:38.687
I'm constantly tired and I
think it's because my body

00:02:38.687 --> 00:02:40.731
is lacking protein.

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:43.415
- Cheated again!

00:02:43.415 --> 00:02:44.715
- It wasn't my fault!

00:02:46.255 --> 00:02:47.500
This guy! Not me!

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.022
- So we realized on day one,

00:02:49.022 --> 00:02:52.505
as (inaudiable) holds a cream
cheese bagel in his hand,

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:55.047
that people were just
going to cheat willy-nilly

00:02:55.047 --> 00:02:57.799
if we didn't have some
kind of rule going on.

00:02:57.799 --> 00:03:01.340
So now, we have a rule where if you cheat,

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.534
you get a punishment.

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:06.517
- Long story short, Justin Tan
had a turkey vegan sandwich,

00:03:06.517 --> 00:03:08.630
or what he thought was
a turkey vegan sandwich,

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:10.512
gave it to me, and was like
"wow, you've got to taste

00:03:10.512 --> 00:03:12.137
this vegan sandwich, it's pretty good."

00:03:12.137 --> 00:03:13.750
- I thought it was vegan!

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.678
- [Ryan] He told me
this sandwich was vegan

00:03:15.678 --> 00:03:17.814
from the (bleep) green vegan truck!

00:03:17.814 --> 00:03:19.008
- As part of Ryan's punishment,

00:03:19.008 --> 00:03:21.702
we got him a veggie burger and then

00:03:21.702 --> 00:03:23.165
Justin will be eating his favorite meal,

00:03:23.165 --> 00:03:24.385
which happens to be...

00:03:24.385 --> 00:03:27.751
- A four-by-four from In-N-Out.

00:03:30.041 --> 00:03:32.059
- Yo! What's up?

00:03:32.059 --> 00:03:33.289
- [Ryan] Are you freaking kidding me?

00:03:33.289 --> 00:03:35.192
What the?

00:03:35.192 --> 00:03:36.772
Wait, are you serious?

00:03:36.772 --> 00:03:37.875
- [Justin] Come on and have a seat, man.

00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:40.011
You have a nice, tasty veggie
burger waiting for you.

00:03:41.741 --> 00:03:42.839
- You piece of (bleep)!

00:03:42.839 --> 00:03:45.585
- Here, I'm going to
take my first bite here.

00:03:45.916 --> 00:03:46.793
Mmm.

00:03:52.539 --> 00:03:54.324
- (Bleep) you.

00:03:54.324 --> 00:03:55.800
- There's an ice cream truck today.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.180
And we can have none of it.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.419
- Yeah, man! Ice cream!

00:04:00.419 --> 00:04:03.017
- Brett Wood. Brett Wood!

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.099
- I'm in the last week of veganism.

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:05.605
And I feel...

00:04:05.605 --> 00:04:07.332
ready for a burger.

00:04:07.332 --> 00:04:09.780
- In the beginning, I was
using a lot of fake meat

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.255
to replace real meat,

00:04:11.255 --> 00:04:14.552
and it was actually making
me feel a lot worse.

00:04:14.552 --> 00:04:17.931
After that, I decided to start
eating more natural food.

00:04:17.931 --> 00:04:19.394
So, more fruits, more veggies,

00:04:19.394 --> 00:04:21.135
and I started to feel a lot better.

00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:22.842
- I do think it's possible
to be a meat eater

00:04:22.842 --> 00:04:26.138
and to use dairy without contributing to

00:04:26.138 --> 00:04:28.332
sort of cruel practices,

00:04:28.332 --> 00:04:30.758
like, there are farms that
treat their animals ethically.

00:04:30.758 --> 00:04:32.360
- In the last week of
this, we are going to

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:33.997
our coworker Caroline's house

00:04:33.997 --> 00:04:36.030
where she's going to cook us a vegan meal

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:36.935
that's actually good.

00:04:36.935 --> 00:04:39.117
She's a vegan expert,
so I'll have a chance

00:04:39.117 --> 00:04:41.364
to eat something that's
not beans and rice.

00:04:44.278 --> 00:04:45.935
(light music)

00:04:47.195 --> 00:04:47.813
- I'm vegan.

00:04:47.813 --> 00:04:49.174
- I'm vegetarian.

00:04:49.174 --> 00:04:51.084
- But an excellent vegan chef.

00:04:51.102 --> 00:04:52.158
A couple of weeks ago, I was talking to

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:56.431
Daysha and Ryan about
what they were eating,

00:04:56.431 --> 00:04:59.123
and it was making me very sad,

00:04:59.123 --> 00:05:01.503
so I wanted to show them
what actual vegan food

00:05:01.503 --> 00:05:02.655
can be like.

00:05:02.655 --> 00:05:03.789
- [Roni] We're going to do yellow curry,

00:05:03.789 --> 00:05:06.007
we're going to do some lard,

00:05:06.007 --> 00:05:08.805
and then a sweet sticky rice,

00:05:08.805 --> 00:05:10.187
coconut, and mango.

00:05:10.187 --> 00:05:11.767
- [Daysha] We're like
where the kids helping out

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:12.684
at Thanksgiving dinner.

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:16.096
- [Roni] Whenever somebody's milling about

00:05:16.096 --> 00:05:19.532
major life choices like
the food you're gonna eat,

00:05:19.532 --> 00:05:21.670
the thing that you really
define your culture by,

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.932
that can be really off-putting
to a lot of people.

00:05:23.932 --> 00:05:26.730
But I think if you show it like this,

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:28.576
that you can make delicious food

00:05:28.576 --> 00:05:30.109
that's not a deprivation,

00:05:30.109 --> 00:05:32.547
I think that's much more
encouraging to people

00:05:32.547 --> 00:05:34.554
to lead a healthier life.

00:05:34.554 --> 00:05:37.354
Maybe the last little
bit is very necessary,

00:05:37.354 --> 00:05:39.454
in our changing environment.

00:05:41.454 --> 00:05:42.506
- I'm no longer vegan.

00:05:42.587 --> 00:05:44.561
It's been one week since
our experiment ended.

00:05:44.561 --> 00:05:45.988
I feel pretty good.

00:05:45.988 --> 00:05:47.428
- It definitely had its highs and lows.

00:05:47.428 --> 00:05:50.447
But overall, I would say
being a vegan wasn't terrible.

00:05:50.447 --> 00:05:51.839
- Going into this, I didn't really know

00:05:51.839 --> 00:05:53.778
what being vegan was about,

00:05:53.778 --> 00:05:55.763
as far as why people do it.

00:05:55.763 --> 00:05:57.180
And now I understand why.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:58.620
It's (bleep)ed up, all
the stuff that we do

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.058
to get the meat that we do.

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:01.627
- Reintroducing meat
and dairy into my diet

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:03.506
wasn't the mind-blowing
thing that I thought

00:06:03.506 --> 00:06:04.321
it was going to be.

00:06:04.321 --> 00:06:06.166
It was just like "oh,
yeah, it's just food."

00:06:06.166 --> 00:06:07.326
- You know, maybe I'll find some

00:06:07.326 --> 00:06:08.604
more ethically raised meat.

00:06:08.604 --> 00:06:10.450
Chipotle serves ethically raised meat.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:13.850
- Your diet is often tied
very closely to your identity

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.324
and your culture, and I
think huge diet changes

00:06:16.324 --> 00:06:18.668
can be really difficult to adopt.

00:06:18.668 --> 00:06:20.701
Not just on a superficial taste level,

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:22.883
but also on an emotional
and a cultural level.

00:06:22.883 --> 00:06:24.577
I sort of have a greater appreciation

00:06:24.577 --> 00:06:27.074
for what goes into my food

00:06:27.074 --> 00:06:28.515
and what goes into my body.

00:06:28.515 --> 00:06:29.814
- I'm just very appreciative of the fact

00:06:29.814 --> 00:06:32.972
that being vegan has helped me feel good

00:06:32.972 --> 00:06:34.667
when eating.

00:06:34.667 --> 00:06:36.050
I think that my whole life,

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:37.848
I've always struggled with food

00:06:37.848 --> 00:06:39.972
and making sure I'm eating right,

00:06:39.972 --> 00:06:43.967
and trying to be a certain size.

00:06:43.967 --> 00:06:45.476
You just learn how to eat right,

00:06:45.476 --> 00:06:48.516
that feeling of feeling
good feels so much better

00:06:48.516 --> 00:06:51.703
than trying to be a certain size.

